1
00:00:00,836 --> 00:00:07,746
This short video shows nurses the Custody page: the custody tools in your clinic, and how to report a faulty tool.

2
00:00:08,196 --> 00:00:12,496
Sign in with your name and password, then tap Custody in the menu.

3
00:00:15,786 --> 00:00:22,486
Scroll down to your clinic. Each tool shows the standard, how many are in the clinic, and any shortage.

4
00:00:22,937 --> 00:00:28,167
Every handpiece has its own serial number, the same number as the sticker on the tool.

5
00:00:28,617 --> 00:00:32,627
If a tool has a problem, tap Report next to its serial number.

6
00:00:33,078 --> 00:00:39,578
Choose the problem: broken, low performance, lost, or other. Write a short description.

7
00:00:40,029 --> 00:00:46,219
Take a photo of the tool. For a broken tool, the photo is required. Then tap Send.

8
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:52,360
The ticket goes to procurement with an email. The tool leaves your clinic count until it comes back.

9
00:00:52,811 --> 00:00:58,163
You can also use the big red button at the top. Choose the clinic, the tool and the unit.

10
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:01,471
If the tool is not registered, write its serial number.

11
00:01:01,922 --> 00:01:08,592
Follow your tickets here: received by procurement, under repair, back in the clinic, or damaged.

12
00:01:09,043 --> 00:01:15,593
That's it. Report any faulty tool right away, so your clinic always has its full set. Thank you!
